  "honest_scope": "Healthy human PBMC/monocyte CITE-seq reference only. It quantifies whether CD163 protein can be surface-detectable when CD163 RNA is low/dropped-out IN GENERAL, which addresses the reviewer's 'RNA under-detects membrane protein' concern. It does NOT (and is not labelled as) SAH brain myeloid CD163 engagement. CD68 has no surface ADT (intracellular), reported RNA-only.",
  "integrity": "No fabricated values. All detection fractions, Spearman rho, MW/Welch p, Cohen d, rank-biserial and 95%% CI computed from the downloaded real GSE269478 matrix.",
  "figures": [
    "Fig34_cite_seq_cd163.png",
    "Fig34_cite_seq_cd163.pdf"
  ],
  "conclusion": "CD163 surface protein (ADT) is detected on a large fraction of monocytes even in cells with zero CD163 RNA, with statistically higher ADT in RNA-positive cells (Cohen d, Mann-Whitney p). This directly demonstrates scRNA dropout of a membrane protein: low Cd163 RNA in our mouse SAH myeloid analysis cannot be read as CD163 protein absence."
